# Agent orientation map

This file is the agent’s working map of the **codebase, behavior, and why it is that way**. It is not the identity/store source of truth.

Use the **Why** section when talking with the user about design (“why no permissions?”, “why return to the start tab?”). If a reason here is wrong or outdated, fix it in the same turn as the code.

## Lookup order (mandatory)

1. **This file** — where to look, how jump/cycle works, design reasons, what not to pack.
2. **`PROJECT.md` / `PROJECT-ru.md`** — only if the task needs names, email, version, listing copy, shortcut, ZIP name, publish status, graphics folders. Prefer `PROJECT-ru.md` when the user writes in Russian.
3. **Named files below** — open those, do not browse the whole repo first.
4. **Search the repo** — only if this map and those files are silent.

Do not start a task by grepping or listing the tree unless the map has no pointer.

`sites/` is a **local sandbox**, not part of the product. Do not open or change it unless the user asks to use or hook it up.

## Keep this map fresh

Update **this file in the same turn** when folders, entry files, jump/cycle logic, permissions, commands, locale keys, ZIP contents, gotchas, **or a design reason** change. Stale map is worse than a short map.

Do **not** copy listing text, publisher name, version, or store URLs here — those live in `PROJECT.md`. If a fact here disagrees with `PROJECT.md`, `PROJECT.md` wins for identity; then fix this map.

No changelogs. Each Why entry is the **current** reason, not history.

## Product (behavior, not marketing)

MV3 toolbar extension. Click the action or `Ctrl+Shift+S` (`Cmd+Shift+S` on Mac, command `jump-to-sound-tab`) → activate the next tab with `tab.audible === true`, focusing its window. No popup, no content scripts, no options page, no network, no storage. Manifest has **no** `permissions` array.

Chrome (`01/`) uses a service worker. Firefox (`firefox/`) uses a non-persistent event page (`background.scripts`). Cycle logic is the same.

